WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:07.860
You touched my hand when I stretched them out so far...

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:18.870
Episode 8

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:18.870
「Illuminated Ground」

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:21.660
Just one word is fine.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.500
Just voice your dreams.

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:28.630
It's your first step and first sign to realization.

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:32.720
Ask yourself what is it that you like?

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:34.840
Your answers will...

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:39.850
blow your questions high into the sky.

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:36.260
Even more...

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:38.140
Like fireworks...

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:46.350
Even though we should all try to be more honest we ourselves, we can't.

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:53.360
Maybe I should try summoning my soul as a child?

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:59.910
What touched my hand when i stretched them out so far...

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:05.040
was a Supernova that suddenly appear to this new night.

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:11.000
For millions of light years, it never stops inside of me.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:19.220
The longer I gaze, the more power my eyes absorb...

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:24.480
and that's because... because I'm a star too!

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:45.910
In a moment, the doors to the 38th Annual Souei High School Culture Festival will be opened.

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.250
Is everyone ready?

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:53.340
Ready when you are!

00:01:58.470 --> 00:01:59.430
It's done.

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:03.260
We did it! We did it!

00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:05.270
All right! We did it!

00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:06.390
We made it in time!

00:02:06.430 --> 00:02:08.020
Yay! Yay!

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:13.110
Our... planetarium...

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:16.650
Star-Shining Astro MAX Star.

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:17.990
What?!

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:19.740
W-W-When did you come up with that name?

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:21.370
It needs to be something a lot cuter!

00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:23.080
How about something simple, like Planet-tan?

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:24.200
Planet-tan?

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:24.990
Planet-tan!

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:27.040
Planet-tan's a really cute name!

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:28.080
Wait, are you sure?

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:30.170
Well, it's easy to say, isn't it?

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:34.000
In that case, Planet-tan it is!

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:44.600
I'm glad that we somehow managed to finish it on time.

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:45.810
Yeah.

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:49.480
You really surprised me when you burst into the room.

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:53.860
I know.

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:56.030
Geez... it's like <i>that</i>, is it?

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:58.440
I put a lot of effort into this.

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:00.570
Well,

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:03.160
I felt like I was God; it felt great.

00:03:03.830 --> 00:03:06.080
Now then, shall I make a star here?

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:08.790
I think I'll make one here just because I feel like it.

00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:10.920
It felt so good...

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:13.080
Everything except for the all-nighter.

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:15.340
I'm very sorry. I'm really grateful.

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:16.460
Look! Look!

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:19.720
After two years, our model of the solar system is finally complete.

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:23.470
Well done, President.

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:25.470
It's amazing! Amazing!

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:42.200
W-What did I just do?!

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:43.410
Please be careful!

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:46.700
The President put a lot of love into making those!

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:52.000
Y-You lot are indeed young...

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:52.960
Sou-nii?!

00:03:54.630 --> 00:03:56.170
Listen up, don't drink this.

00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:59.210
You can all still recover naturally.

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:01.300
You should stay away from drinks like this...

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:03.300
If you're interested, I'd just leave it as that.

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:08.720
Luckily, us teachers have almost nothing to do on the actual day.

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:10.980
If necessary, I can go and sleep in my car.

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:14.350
Oh, no! I was supposed to be with the Photography Club by now!

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:16.940
Hime-Hime! Do my make up!

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:20.280
Ah, that means we're rivals now.

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:24.570
Have you all forgotten? The best event competition?

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:27.120
Oh, that's right!

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:34.620
They're presents from me to you.

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:37.840
Well, I guess you could say they're kind of like uniforms.

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:39.090
Souma-sensei...

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:42.260
There's one for me too!

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:43.590
I'm so happy!

00:04:43.630 --> 00:04:46.180
Well, you're a member of our club in all but name, really.

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:49.680
What's more, the stars are positioned in a really nice place.

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:55.350
Well then, everyone,

00:04:59.110 --> 00:05:01.900
let's win the best event competition!

00:05:02.030 --> 00:05:04.610
Let's aim for a full house!

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:09.450
Thank you for visiting us.

00:05:09.950 --> 00:05:16.500
Every year, we hold a best classroom or club event competition.

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:24.550
Please place the marble you receive upon entry into the ballot box of the event you think should win.

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:28.090
There are an incredible number of people even though it's still morning.

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:29.600
All right!

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:31.890
Attack!

00:05:37.980 --> 00:05:42.360
Building C might be a little far, but if we can start a stream of people heading that way...

00:05:49.030 --> 00:05:49.990
Hello-

00:05:50.070 --> 00:05:51.780
Saku! Saku!

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:52.450
It's Mary!

00:05:52.490 --> 00:05:53.580
Mary's here!

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:57.960
Oscar!

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:57.920
[Note: Mary and Oscar are from the musical, "The Rose of Versailles."]

00:05:58.540 --> 00:06:00.420
Oscar!

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:01.750
This?!

00:06:02.710 --> 00:06:04.460
Do none of the events interest you?

00:06:05.510 --> 00:06:08.760
In that case, just watch our stage.

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:14.930
This year, the Movie Club is holding a 2-hour play...

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:19.230
...called Eikenja!

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:19.230
[Note: "Eikenja" translates to "We're the Movie Club." The "ja" makes the name sound similar to "Power Rangers."]

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:22.320
If it's that long, we won't be able to see the other events.

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:23.320
What?!

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:30.450
Class A 3-2 will captivate the hearts of mothers with its beautiful boys.

00:06:34.950 --> 00:06:36.830
Don't underestimate the sport clubs' food booths!

00:06:36.950 --> 00:06:39.290
Behold, our well-trained left-turn-overs!

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:48.300
A battlefield...

00:06:49.630 --> 00:06:50.890
This place is a battlefield...

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:57.680
Ah! Our President's withdrawn into himself!

00:06:57.890 --> 00:06:59.390
No, he hasn't.

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:00.650
This is-

00:07:01.850 --> 00:07:05.520
Stars are so nice... Romantic~

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:10.740
Have you heard about the Las Vegas room in Building C?

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:15.240
Everyone, gather around. It's a planetarium~

00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:16.200
A jingle?!

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:18.040
But he's so gloomy!

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:21.460
President, you need to be more cheerful! More cheerful!

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:24.670
No one seems to be coming.

00:07:25.500 --> 00:07:27.170
I wonder if everyone's okay.

00:07:27.590 --> 00:07:29.970
Do you think we should've gone too?

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:33.430
Ciao!

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:34.850
Haruko-san!

00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:34.850
Haruko-san!

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:38.600
What?! They're hosting a planetarium?

00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:40.520
How nice.

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:45.110
What? We can even see it before the Theater Club's play?

00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:49.280
It might be a better idea than just walking around getting tired.

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:50.280
Let's see.

00:07:50.530 --> 00:07:51.820
It says here that there's a planetarium.

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:55.660
You're fantastic as always, Haruko-san!

00:07:56.330 --> 00:07:58.450
Now then, let's do the rest without resorting to trickery.

00:07:58.740 --> 00:07:59.660
Ooyagi-kun!

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:01.910
Yoshinari-san. Izumi-san.

00:08:02.710 --> 00:08:03.920
We've come to help you.

00:08:04.420 --> 00:08:06.710
But isn't the Literature Club busy with lectures and such?

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:07.750
Don't worry.

00:08:08.210 --> 00:08:11.220
Kotodzuka-senpai asked us to.

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:13.050
She did?

00:08:13.340 --> 00:08:13.760
Yup.

00:08:15.260 --> 00:08:16.760
Oh, Ooyagi-san.

00:08:18.220 --> 00:08:20.020
Miku-chan! Rena-chan!

00:08:20.350 --> 00:08:21.350
H-Hello.

00:08:22.060 --> 00:08:23.100
You guys came.

00:08:23.390 --> 00:08:23.940
Yup.

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:26.310
Oh, they're Edogawa's younger sisters.

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:29.110
What?!

00:08:30.230 --> 00:08:31.860
Well, I'll show you where Edogawa is.

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:32.700
Oh, thank you.

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:33.200
Okay!

00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:40.410
I'm amazed that Edogawa-kun has such cute sisters.

00:08:40.830 --> 00:08:41.580
Yeah...

00:08:41.910 --> 00:08:44.120
But right now, isn't Edogawa-kun...

00:08:57.010 --> 00:08:58.600
Ew!

00:08:58.640 --> 00:09:01.060
No! No family members allowed!

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:03.640
Stupid brother!

00:09:08.270 --> 00:09:09.520
I'm sorry, Edogawa.

00:09:09.610 --> 00:09:10.690
Hime, hurry.

00:09:11.030 --> 00:09:12.490
The dressing squad is waiting for you.

00:09:12.650 --> 00:09:14.110
I know!

00:09:19.530 --> 00:09:20.620
Makita-san!

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:25.790
Thanks for the diary!

00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:28.500
Thanks to that, I was somehow able to help out!

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:32.550
And... how should I say this... it made me happy!

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:34.590
Thank you!

00:09:42.810 --> 00:09:44.270
Oh?

00:09:45.020 --> 00:09:46.770
I-It's nothing.

00:09:46.850 --> 00:09:47.600
Come on. We're going.

00:09:47.690 --> 00:09:49.020
Hime!

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:50.270
Wait!

00:09:54.280 --> 00:09:56.070
There's a stream of people.

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:01.990
Excuse me-

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:04.450
Come in. Come in.

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:06.870
Wow! It looks like an igloo!

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:08.500
It looks strange.

00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:09.880
So you watch from in there?

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:12.000
It looks interesting.

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:12.000
Amazing.

00:10:12.590 --> 00:10:14.510
We will begin shortly.

00:10:15.050 --> 00:10:17.680
Please take off your shoes and enter.

00:10:25.890 --> 00:10:28.230
Our show will be "Tonight's Sky."

00:10:30.690 --> 00:10:31.610
So, it's begun.

00:10:32.150 --> 00:10:33.900
In there, right now, it's night.

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:36.650
But I wonder if Mihoshi-chan will be okay.

00:10:37.240 --> 00:10:40.030
One person does everything, so it's a fairly tough job.

00:10:41.740 --> 00:10:42.830
She'll be fine.

00:10:44.030 --> 00:10:48.160
A good way to find the North Star is to first find the Cassiopeia constellation

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:52.130
which is shaped like a W, making it easy to spot.

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:57.630
Glowing dimly beside it, is the Kepheus constellation.

00:10:58.090 --> 00:11:01.890
You should be able to visualize a king and queen standing next to one another.

00:11:03.100 --> 00:11:06.270
Oh! A hand-made planetarium.

00:11:06.770 --> 00:11:08.310
It sure brings back memories.

00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:09.890
Principal...

00:11:10.850 --> 00:11:13.610
More to the point, we have an astronomy club?

00:11:13.860 --> 00:11:14.520
Yes.

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:20.240
I once made a desktop planetarium myself.

00:11:21.740 --> 00:11:22.660
Principal...

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:27.240
Please visit me at the Kosugino City Children's Space Science Museum.

00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:29.120
Groups are welcome too.

00:11:29.210 --> 00:11:30.710
Haruko-san, are you advertising?!

00:11:33.750 --> 00:11:35.540
That was amazing! Amazing!

00:11:35.540 --> 00:11:37.840
It was a lot more realistic than I had anticipated.

00:11:38.590 --> 00:11:40.880
The guide had a really cute voice.

00:11:41.470 --> 00:11:43.010
It was beautiful.

00:11:43.010 --> 00:11:43.720
Yeah.

00:11:43.720 --> 00:11:45.350
Maybe I'll take a look outside tonight.

00:11:48.350 --> 00:11:50.390
Now then, the next group's waiting for you.

00:11:50.680 --> 00:11:54.150
Saku, Mom is so touched!

00:11:55.360 --> 00:11:57.190
I'm sorry. I overslept-

00:12:00.610 --> 00:12:02.280
Hello, I'm Haruko.

00:12:06.410 --> 00:12:09.410
If you open your heart~

00:12:09.500 --> 00:12:11.710
Are you getting hungry?

00:12:13.710 --> 00:12:15.630
Eikenja is here!

00:12:18.340 --> 00:12:20.460
Thank you!

00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:22.800
Oscar!

00:12:35.230 --> 00:12:37.860
Thank you very much for coming today.

00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:39.860
It was a wonderful lecture.

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:41.860
The honor's all mine.

00:12:42.740 --> 00:12:44.530
This year's magazine was as wonderful as always.

00:12:45.160 --> 00:12:46.070
This too.

00:12:46.370 --> 00:12:49.620
The direction taken is different than your usual style, but I enjoyed it a lot.

00:12:54.460 --> 00:12:55.580
Thank you very much.

00:12:56.040 --> 00:12:57.290
I'm sure everyone will be happy to hear that.

00:12:58.090 --> 00:12:59.840
It was wonderful.

00:12:58.090 --> 00:12:59.840
It was amazing.

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:01.510
I never knew you could make your own.

00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:03.220
I think they were our last group.

00:13:03.800 --> 00:13:05.090
Yes, probably.

00:13:09.010 --> 00:13:10.470
N-Nothing...

00:13:11.560 --> 00:13:16.100
Come to think of it, I haven't talked to her properly since I came back.

00:13:17.560 --> 00:13:18.940
Is it over already?

00:13:23.110 --> 00:13:23.740
Um...

00:13:24.070 --> 00:13:27.490
Geez... it's because you were so slow, Hiro-kun.

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:29.870
I-I'm sorry.

00:13:32.490 --> 00:13:33.950
It's fine. Do you want to take a look?

00:13:34.080 --> 00:13:35.040
Really?

00:13:34.160 --> 00:13:35.040
Really?

00:13:35.250 --> 00:13:35.660
Yup.

00:13:36.420 --> 00:13:37.420
Where are your Mommy and Daddy?

00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:38.960
We came by ourselves.

00:13:39.380 --> 00:13:40.670
We live close by.

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:46.590
Saku-chan, you too.

00:13:53.020 --> 00:13:54.640
There are stars on my body!

00:13:54.890 --> 00:13:56.190
It's so pretty!

00:13:56.770 --> 00:13:58.350
It's amazing, isn't it?

00:14:05.860 --> 00:14:08.410
Saku-chan, thank you.

00:14:09.160 --> 00:14:12.330
Really, really thank you.

00:14:13.950 --> 00:14:15.500
Narrowly avoiding the closure of the club...

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:19.420
...and stargazing with Fumin during our summer outing...

00:14:20.330 --> 00:14:23.340
It's all... It's all thanks to you.

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:26.050
Even with the preparations for the Cultural Festival...

00:14:27.550 --> 00:14:29.590
...you worked hard by yourself in the Literature Club.

00:14:31.390 --> 00:14:32.100
Yet...

00:14:33.140 --> 00:14:38.190
Yet, I felt sad.

00:14:39.560 --> 00:14:44.150
I told myself that it was only until you finished helping them.

00:14:45.820 --> 00:14:46.900
That I needed to do my best till then...

00:14:50.030 --> 00:14:50.740
But...

00:14:51.780 --> 00:14:52.910
But I'm glad.

00:14:54.540 --> 00:14:56.160
I'm glad that I didn't trouble you.

00:14:59.830 --> 00:15:00.540
That's...

00:15:04.550 --> 00:15:07.760
...not why I did that.

00:15:09.720 --> 00:15:12.510
Will we be able to see this tonight?

00:15:12.800 --> 00:15:14.100
What are they called?

00:15:14.890 --> 00:15:15.560
Yup.

00:15:15.970 --> 00:15:18.140
I'll tell you about every single one of them.

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:44.130
It feels like autumn now that the Cultural Festival's over...

00:15:44.750 --> 00:15:48.630
"Akimeku"... "tokimeku," "tokimekimekitoki"...

00:15:48.630 --> 00:15:50.720
Zoning out is no excuse for rhyming!

00:15:51.010 --> 00:15:53.430
It was too bad about the best event competition.

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:55.850
We didn't even make it into the top three...

00:15:56.010 --> 00:15:58.350
I thought that we might've had a chance at it.

00:15:59.020 --> 00:16:00.640
A lot of people did come to our event.

00:16:01.190 --> 00:16:02.440
Thank you everyone!

00:16:01.480 --> 00:16:04.520
It's like the popular clubs stormed through...

00:16:02.480 --> 00:16:04.650
We, the Photography Club, came third!

00:16:02.520 --> 00:16:04.650
We're the Brass Band. We came second.

00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:07.690
Telescope...

00:16:07.150 --> 00:16:09.070
I wanted to be able to get one as a group...

00:16:09.190 --> 00:16:10.650
Erm... did I remind you?

00:16:11.030 --> 00:16:12.070
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

00:16:12.280 --> 00:16:14.780
Also, we still need to take down Planet-tan...

00:16:21.370 --> 00:16:22.830
Ready, everyone?

00:16:23.330 --> 00:16:24.920
On three!

00:16:30.630 --> 00:16:32.010
Let's go!

00:16:32.380 --> 00:16:34.760
One... two... three!

00:16:38.100 --> 00:16:40.890
I knew it! I just can't take it apart!

00:16:41.020 --> 00:16:43.230
Planet-tan!

00:16:47.520 --> 00:16:49.570
Hey, is everyone here?

00:16:49.860 --> 00:16:50.940
Sou-nii!

00:16:52.190 --> 00:16:52.900
What's wrong with you all?

00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:54.610
You all seem unusually depressed.

00:16:55.740 --> 00:16:59.240
We were just reminiscing about the festival since we miss it so much.

00:16:59.490 --> 00:17:00.620
Ah, I see.

00:17:00.830 --> 00:17:03.620
I understand that, but you need to get over it.

00:17:05.120 --> 00:17:07.580
I know that, but...

00:17:08.170 --> 00:17:08.420
Hm? What's that?

00:17:08.670 --> 00:17:11.420
Saku-kun, you're reading a book by Nojiri Houei?

00:17:12.090 --> 00:17:13.420
That's a good book you're reading.

00:17:13.970 --> 00:17:18.510
You... said I should read more books on Astronomy...

00:17:19.010 --> 00:17:19.640
Which is why I...

00:17:24.310 --> 00:17:28.310
Well, yeah, but I had something a little different in mind.

00:17:28.770 --> 00:17:30.730
Well, I guess that will do for now.

00:17:30.940 --> 00:17:31.780
It's just like you.

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:33.360
Let's do what suits you best.

00:17:35.360 --> 00:17:36.820
Hey, Astronomy Club!

00:17:37.660 --> 00:17:39.990
What's this pile in the middle of the hallway?

00:17:40.080 --> 00:17:42.240
We found them selling really cheaply at the bazaar.

00:17:42.330 --> 00:17:43.200
They're discounted items!

00:17:43.040 --> 00:17:44.500
That's beside the point!

00:17:45.620 --> 00:17:48.420
I was planning to give you some credit, but now that I'm faced with this...

00:17:49.130 --> 00:17:50.420
The planetarium was excellent.

00:17:50.880 --> 00:17:53.050
My family said they visited too.

00:17:53.130 --> 00:17:53.760
Haraguchi!

00:17:54.300 --> 00:17:56.510
Anyway, make sure you do things properly!

00:17:56.970 --> 00:17:57.880
We're very sorry.

00:17:58.140 --> 00:17:59.470
Let's go, Haraguchi.

00:18:00.010 --> 00:18:00.640
Okay.

00:18:02.930 --> 00:18:04.270
Oh yeah, your parent's-

00:18:08.600 --> 00:18:10.730
Fumin's words gave me a dose of reality!

00:18:10.730 --> 00:18:12.020
Thank you, Fumin!

00:18:12.480 --> 00:18:16.530
Long nights, fresh air, and lots and lots of myths!

00:18:16.780 --> 00:18:19.200
The best stargazing season starts now!

00:18:19.200 --> 00:18:21.070
Yet, how could I?!

00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:22.870
Saku-chan, let's go tonight!

00:18:22.910 --> 00:18:24.580
Let's stargaze tonight!

00:18:24.580 --> 00:18:25.790
With these futons!

00:18:25.500 --> 00:18:26.830
Calm down!

00:18:29.370 --> 00:18:33.250
Old lady, why don't we all go together?

00:18:33.840 --> 00:18:35.300
Then, why don't we watch the moon?

00:18:36.510 --> 00:18:38.550
We weren't able to do that during the Mid-Autumn Moon Festival

00:18:38.510 --> 00:18:39.800
because we were in the midst of our Cultural Festival,

00:18:40.300 --> 00:18:43.310
but since this seems like a good opportunity, I'd like to watch the moon.

00:18:43.470 --> 00:18:45.970
I completely forgot about that.

00:18:52.610 --> 00:18:56.230
Sayo-senpai, your house is a temple?

00:18:56.530 --> 00:18:56.940
Yup.

00:18:57.280 --> 00:19:01.070
It's our first stargazing session in a while, so please make yourselves at home.

00:19:02.280 --> 00:19:04.410
Oh my, Sayo-chan, welcome back.

00:19:04.530 --> 00:19:06.410
Good afternoon, Granny Tajima.

00:19:06.540 --> 00:19:09.960
It sure is lively. Are they your friends?

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:12.170
They're from the Astronomy Club. They're here to watch the moon.

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:12.080
Somehow, she fits in with this place...

00:19:12.250 --> 00:19:13.090
Why?

00:19:13.170 --> 00:19:16.250
Why isn't it a shrine?

00:19:17.920 --> 00:19:20.930
Sayo! Mihoshi-chan!

00:19:21.010 --> 00:19:22.800
Welcome home!

00:19:23.600 --> 00:19:25.470
Why did you dodge me, Sayo?

00:19:25.640 --> 00:19:27.140
You ought to learn from Mihoshi-chan!

00:19:27.020 --> 00:19:29.690
Dad, there are temple followers watching you!

00:19:31.100 --> 00:19:34.360
Sayo, who are these men?

00:19:34.730 --> 00:19:36.980
Are you the eldest son? The sole son?

00:19:37.150 --> 00:19:39.820
Erm... no, it's me Souma. Don't you remember me?

00:19:40.030 --> 00:19:41.410
I'm the second son.

00:19:40.820 --> 00:19:41.410
I'm the only son.

00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:42.410
I'm the eldest son.

00:19:42.450 --> 00:19:45.280
Then, go home!

00:19:53.080 --> 00:19:54.210
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:20:01.220 --> 00:20:03.050
Sayo!

00:20:04.300 --> 00:20:08.930
Dad will eat everything you've cooked.

00:20:08.220 --> 00:20:09.350
Dad!

00:20:13.980 --> 00:20:15.900
The moon rise is at 22:00.

00:20:16.940 --> 00:20:19.480
The fukemachidzuki, eh?

00:20:16.980 --> 00:20:19.480
[Note: "Fukemachidzuki" is another name for the moon festival that occurs on the 20th of August.]

00:20:19.990 --> 00:20:22.530
The summer constellations can still be seen,

00:20:22.990 --> 00:20:25.320
but before we've even realized, the air's completely different.

00:20:27.580 --> 00:20:29.240
It's rising!

00:20:30.790 --> 00:20:35.210
The moon near the horizon is sort of reddish and big... it's almost scary.

00:20:35.830 --> 00:20:40.090
But it's the exact same moon we can see in the sky that's by the horizon now.

00:20:40.260 --> 00:20:41.170
No way!

00:20:41.760 --> 00:20:47.600
Disembark on the sea of moisture, travel past the Bullialdus to the Sea of Islands.

00:20:48.430 --> 00:20:53.730
Cross the Copernicus, circle the Sea of Showers, and into the inlet of the Lunik Bay.

00:20:54.730 --> 00:20:58.900
If we had a telescope, we could have seen all the ins and outs of the craters.

00:21:00.320 --> 00:21:01.530
Telescope...

00:21:01.780 --> 00:21:04.450
Because we're were no good...

00:21:05.360 --> 00:21:08.120
We can't imagine it because we've never seen one.

00:21:08.280 --> 00:21:08.700
Yup.

00:21:09.700 --> 00:21:12.580
Well, the Astronomy Club's just starting.

00:21:19.040 --> 00:21:22.050
Oh yeah, we received a parcel for the Astronomy Club.

00:21:25.090 --> 00:21:26.680
Nogishiro High School?

00:21:27.090 --> 00:21:28.010
The school that's in the same prefecture as us?

00:21:33.350 --> 00:21:34.230
Hello.

00:21:34.810 --> 00:21:36.480
My name is Oumi.

00:21:36.730 --> 00:21:38.730
I am the President of Nogishiro High School's Astronomy Club.

00:21:39.520 --> 00:21:42.690
I'm sure I must have surprised you with our sudden video letter,

00:21:43.530 --> 00:21:48.620
but we saw your event at your Cultural Festival the other day.

00:21:49.320 --> 00:21:54.500
I was very surprised because I can't recall seeing any such events in previous years.

00:21:55.460 --> 00:21:59.080
Therefore, I would like you to consider participating

00:21:59.750 --> 00:22:03.840
in the Prefecture High School Astronomy Network's periodic stargazing session.

00:22:04.590 --> 00:22:05.380
Prefecture...

00:22:05.800 --> 00:22:06.680
...High School...

00:22:06.680 --> 00:22:07.840
...Astronomy...

00:22:08.260 --> 00:22:09.640
...Network?

00:22:10.550 --> 00:22:13.520
I will await your response.

00:22:22.400 --> 00:22:26.780
I look up at the sky, and I think of you…

00:22:27.070 --> 00:22:30.450
but I can’t find the words,

00:22:31.580 --> 00:22:33.740
I want to tell you,

00:22:33.740 --> 00:22:36.250
but they just slip away…

00:22:36.580 --> 00:22:39.920
almost like Shooting Stars.

00:22:40.420 --> 00:22:44.500
In this Wave of Silence,

00:22:44.880 --> 00:22:48.880
a ray of light flickers the darkness

00:22:49.340 --> 00:22:54.180
playing with my memories

00:22:54.180 --> 00:23:00.020
and releasing my heart.

00:23:00.850 --> 00:23:02.980
Into the future,

00:23:02.980 --> 00:23:11.530
I will have these feelings again!

00:23:11.950 --> 00:23:15.950
No worries, I’m not alone.

00:23:16.200 --> 00:23:21.040
You have taught me I’m not alone.

00:23:21.040 --> 00:23:29.970
Listen to my “Twinkle” story!

00:23:30.090 --> 00:23:34.140
Maybe my voice would reach you.

00:23:35.510 --> 00:23:40.390
I look up at the sky, surrounded by Stardust!

00:23:45.610 --> 00:23:47.150
Next time, on Sora no Manimani:

00:23:47.480 --> 00:23:48.940
High School Astronomy Network.
